      "claim": "Rumi’s poetry (Divan‑e‑Shams, Masnavi) contains numerous verses expressing longing, separation (*ḥijr*), and spiritual anguish, showing his inner life was not dominated by constant joy.",
      "evidence": "Scholarly analyses (e.g., Kabir 2010; D. G. H. *Rumi’s Poetic Themes*) highlight ghazals and masnavis of sorrow and yearning.",
